	One follow on to my earlier remarks about VMS was that there was
some administrativia that I recall about opening data files under DEC-
FORTRAN, which was/is a very good F77 with extensions, data structures.
It was that you had to open files with some modes from some package called
RMS. It was a royal pain to have to plead with the OS to open an ascii
file under some rules for dealing with the format of the data in the
file. I think that UNIX's notion is vastly superior than dealing with
files with physical blocksizes that you had to obey when you open and
read and then write files. This must be a throwback to OS/JCL which I
also once had exposure to. It is brain-dead. 

Bruce Salem

