In article <688@bsjlgw.barclays.co.jp>, masahiro@barclays.co.jp (Masahiro Yanagisawa) writes:
|>What is the GIGAswitch ?

The GIGAswitch is a fast crossbar FDDI switch.  If you're familiar with Kalpana,
think of the GIGAswitch as the same, except on FDDI.  In actuality, the
GIGAswitch has some very advanced features such as full-duplex support on each
port (>100Mbps), redundant power supplies, modular PMD cards (UTP, MM, SM),
upcoming ATM line card support, etc.

|>Is there any FAQs for the GIGAswitch ?
|>Is there any contact person to get the GIGAswitch ?

Try contacting your local Digital salesperson for more information, or call
1-603-884-6660 (USA) for the Digital contact in your area.  There is also
information available on Digital's anonymous FTP server (gatekeeper.dec.com)
in /pub/DEC/DECinfo/infosheet/gigaswitch.txt.

