We've experienced this problem on two of our Alpha 3000s (400 and 500) 
running OpenVMS 1.5 and Motif.  At some seemingly arbitrary point in time
on a console monitor window, the keyboard goes into a mode where every
other keystroke is normal but the alternate stroke activates the Delete
key (<X) which repeats continuously until one types another key. 
Therefore, all window sessions are no longer useful and the process has
to be killed from another login.  A reboot solved the problem, but a new
keyboard (DEC's attempt) didn't.  I haven't seen it happen often enough
to try this, but I imagine that one could restart the window manager to
allow logins on the console monitor.  I haven't found out yet if one
particular user has possibly remapped the keyboard, but it doesn't seem
likely, since every OTHER keystroke is causing the problem! 

One suggestion was a driver bug, but DEC hasn't been much help thus far.
Anyone out there have an answer?  Sorry, but this was cross-posted with 
vmsnet.alpha.

