List-directed input from an internal file (and output to an internal file)
is an extension to Fortran 77 that is supported by all DEC Fortran
implementations.  I tried it on a DEC OSF/1 AXP system and it worked as I
expected.  If you're having a problem on that platform, please send me a
copy of the source, the version of DEC Fortran installed (from a listing
header), and a log showing the results. 

Here's my test case:

 $ cat ldx.f
       CHARACTER*10  LINE
       LINE = '12345'
       READ (LINE,*) L
       TYPE *,L
       END
 $ f77 -o ldx ldx.f
 $ ldx
       12345
-- 

