In article <37472@dog.ee.lbl.gov>, ctday@randolf.lbl.gov (Christopher T. Day) writes:
> Can anyone tell me the ANSI standard status of list directed I/O (I in
> particular)
> from internal files in FORTRAN 77?
> I can't find anything in my FORTRAN 77 book forbidding it or allowing
> non-support as an option; I infer that it should be allowed. My FORTRAN
> 90 book positively recommends it as an effective programming technique.
> What's the official word? It's making ports a bit of a pain. (Short term,
> is there a way to get the AXP system to accept the idea?) Thanks.

List-directed formatting to/from an internal file is not standard Fortran
77, but it is standard Fortran 90.  Some Fortran 77 compilers allow it as
an extension.

I wouldn't infer that something is allowed just because a text doesn't
mention it.  My assumption is always "if it doesn't say you can, assume you
can't."

