In order to move the files from VMS, you need to know something about the
file type under VMS, which you can see using "DIR/FULL filespec".  You can
make an ANSI tape using the COPY command, as in "INIT MUA0: label",
"MOUNT MUA0: label", "COPY filespec MUA0:*".  The blocksize can be varied
by using a qualifier in COPY.

The format of the data on tape will depend on the VMS file type.  One way 
you can look at the tape is to use DUMP under VMS.  A typical tape format
is 4 bytes of record length, followed by a record, padded to next even
location. "^^^^" ends a tape record.
