In article <CLLz40.AMs@murdoch.acc.Virginia.EDU>, sam3a@uvacs.cs.Virginia.EDU
(Sally A. McKee) writes:
|>I just started working with the alpha (21064). Unfortunately,
|>I have precious little documentation at my disposal, and it
|>all seems to be older than the machine. I'd like to find out
|>1) how big the L2 cache is, and
|>2) details of the memory system (what kind of components,
|>	access/cycle times, special modes . . .)
|>
|>Everything I've read says that the size of the L2 cache can
|>vary. Is there a standard configuration? Or is there some
|>(easy) way I can find out what my configuration is? I found
|>out how much memory we've got by looking at the boot log,
|>but it says nothing about caches.

   The DECchip 21064 is an implementation of the Alpha Architecture. 
   AXP is the name given to Alpha Architecture systems sold by Digital.

   Neither the DECchip 21064 nor the Alpha architecture includes a
   specific size requirement for the secondary cache.  In other words,
   the size of the secondary cache (if any -- though all current AXP
   systems do have it) (and the specific DECchip 2106x MHz) is system
   (or implementation) dependent.

   The DECchip 21064 has an 8 KByte Instruction and an 8 KByte Data
   cache located on-chip. Secondary Cache for various AXP models:

     DEC 2000-300, DECpc AXP 150: 512 KByte
     DEC 3000-600, 3000-600S, 3000-800, 3000-800S: 2 MByte
     DEC 4000-600: 1 Mbyte per processor
     DEC 4000-800, 7000-600, 10000-600: 4 Mbyte per processor

   If your particular machine is not included on the above list, please
   indicate the particular model AXP.

   The DECchip 21064a doubles the DECchip 21064 primary cache sizes, and
   it runs at an increased MHz.  (225 and 275 MHz) 

   Further details of the memory subsystems _should_ be in the CPU-specific
   technical manual for the particular implementation.
   
   For additional information, please send mail to info@digital.com. 
   (This mailserver will reply with the various services, systems and
   sorts of information available from Digital.)   (Digital's DECchip
   information line is 508-568-5409; Eastern Time.)

