In article <760977505snz@brendata.demon.co.uk> steveh@brendata.demon.co.uk (Steve J Hanselman) writes:
> I need to increase the size of the driver partition on one of our trusty
> RSX machines, as we have changed the type of magtape.
> My memory fades, but I have edited the SYSVMR.CMD file,
> I recall that you do something like VMR @SYSVMR,
> but would some kind PDP owner like to post exactly
> what I need to do?

Yep, copy RSX11M.TSK to RSX11M.SYS. I hate this bit, so I protect the .tsk
file to RO for the day I get it wrong... ;-)

Then do your VMR @SYSVMR. BTW, you may want to install stuff there
instead of in startup and get some contiguous pool back.

Then boot your new system. I set the date to when I VMRed it, so I can
correctly forget what I did. HAte to forget the wrong details by mistake.
Then you save your system and write the boot block. If it is an I/D M-PLUS
system, the book should say SAV/WB/MOU="/ACP=unique/win=full/ext=40/lru=20
/vi" This will give the system a nice boost in performance.

If you run Decnet, you can VMR in Decnet as well, and set up the net with
VNP. ( Be careful. VNP is very good at trashing system images. ) You
can power on and be on the net in ~45 seconds that way. :-)

Mail if problems. Or you need manual info.

