Recently we installed a WangDAT 3400DX on a VAXstation 4000/VLC running
VMS 5.5. The WangDAT 3400DX supports data compression (media compaction),
this increases the tape capacity and also improves the write speed.

When we do a INITIALIZE/MEDIA_FORMAT=COMPACTION, then SHOW DEVICE/FULL
show that compaction is enabled, however once the tape is mounted, either
with MOUNT or directly by BACKUP --- the compaction is *disabled* !!!
("controller supports compaction (compaction  disabled)")
The drive is set up to use compaction by default, so this means that VMS
sends a Mode Select on the SCSI bus that disables this feature.

Is this just the way things are, or is there a way to get the full benefit
of this drive? (Apart from moving it to a Unix box?) Does only compaction
work on DEC drives? Is the answer "upgrade to VMS 6.0"?

Any clues?

-psi (PerSteinar.Iversen@filuib.no) 




