castor@drizzle.Stanford.EDU (Castor Fu) writes:

>I don't know if the problem is strictly with the AXP driver.  I 
>tried plugging the keyboard (LK401-AA Rev C01) into a decsttion 5000,
>and had the same problems.   I couldn't reproduce the error with
>an LK401-AA Rev A02.


  There have been sporatic reports of autorepeat problems, I have at
  least one that I am looking at for OpenVMS AXP.  I'd be interested
  to know if you are seeing them on OSF/1 as well.

  The general problem is that X11 wants the keyboard to be in specific
  modes that are not the default modes for the keyboard (the LK200
  having been invented long before X11, and the LK400 being SW
  compatable).  If the KB gets into a state that is different than
  what the driver thinks it's in... then you get these type of
  problems.  It's *much* harder to get into this type state on OSF/1.

  One way this can happen is if you have a flakey KB, KB connector,
  or connector wire - such that some or all of the commands sent to
  the keyboard from the system are not seen.  The driver will then
  believe that the keyboard modes have been set - and you will end up
  with certain keys autorepeating (delete, arrows, etc).

  I don't know any problems that would be specific to the 3000-300
  series - if it happens to one, it would happen to them all.  It
  may be that you just have a flakey KB.

