I am pleased to announce the first availability of a DEC Fortran for OpenVMS
VAX Systems "patch kit" on the Internet via FTP.  The version currently
available, V6.1-101, contains changes and corrections not included in the
"SSB" release V6.1-68 which began shipping in October.

There are a couple of new features in this version that may be of interest.
The first is that the compiler now treats as comments source lines which
contain # in column 1.  This allows the use of the VAX C preprocessor on
Fortran source; previously, the compiler would reject such lines which
are created by the VAX C preprocessor.  A second feature is a new
directive, CDEC$ ALIAS, which allows you to specify an alternate external
name for a called function or subroutine.  This can ease migration of
sources between UNIX systems, which generally add an underscore for
Fortran routine global names, and OpenVMS.

The release notes are, as usual, included in the kit; please see them
for more details.  Also, watch for an announcement regarding FTP
availability of current release notes for most Digital compiler products.

To obtain the kit, use anonymous FTP and connect to gatekeeper.dec.com
(16.1.0.2) and look in pub/DEC/FORTRAN.  The kit is in ZIP format; if
you don't have UNZIP, you'll find UNZIP-VAX.EXE in that directory.  The
V6.1-101 kit is called FORTRAN-VAX-VMS-061-101.ZIP.  Use IMAGE mode when
copying the files.

To unpack the kit, use the following commands:

	$ UNZIP :== $disk:[dir]UNZIP-VAX
	$ UNZIP FORTRAN-VAX-VMS-061-101

This will create FORT061.A which is a normal VMSINSTAL-able saveset.
Note that you must have a license and Product Authorization Key for
DEC Fortran V6.1 to use this update.

It is our intention to provide additional update kits through this
medium; please let me know if you have any problems obtaining or 
using the kit.
