extra info:

What you need is version 3.0 or higher of the infoserver software.
With that version you can create mop services no only on filename, for 
decservers, but also for ethernet addresses.

Look on page 5 of the VXT software version 2.0 release notes.
There is an section about booting vt1300 terminals with infoserver version 3.0 
software.
Also look in the System Operation guide for infoserver software version 3.0 
chapter 4.9.1 (page 4-11)

"quoted for VXT software version 2.0 release notes"

Infoserver Version 3.0 software lets you associate an Ethernet address with a 
partition for MOP loading functions. This feature is useful for VT1300 
terminals. You can use this feature to load the VXT loader or the VXT EX image 
in host0based mode.

To use this feature, you must create a permanent partition on the InfoServer 
system for each image to be served this way. After you install VXT software, 
copy the desired VXT software imgae to a private partition. You must perform 
these steps each time you update the VXT software.

>>SHOW PART DK1:VXTLDR			(To see the size of this partition<<

EXAMPLE:

SET SERVER STATE OFF
CREATE PARTITION DK1:VT1300_LOADER BLOCK 1000
COPY DK1:VXTLDR020.SYS DK1:VT1300_LOADER
SET SERVER STATE ON
CREATE SERVICE MOP$08002B112233 FOR DK1:VT1300_LOADER CLASS MOP
CREATE PARTITION DK1:XXXXZZZZ BLOCKS 10
DELETE PARTITION DK1:XXXXZZZZ
SAVE

Note: the creation and deletion of partition xxxxzzzz above is a temporary 
workaraound for infoserver version 3.0 software. For more information see 
Section 4.9

4.9 That dummy partition causes the infoserver system to flush its internal 
cache and complete the creation of any other MOP partition, to be corrected in a 
later version of infoserver software

