Users need to use the Motif "customize security" option and add in the DECnet
address (not name) of the node they wish to allow to connect.  This is because
when the EWS software runs, it speaks DECnet but does not have a known-nodes
database to use to translate DECnet addresses into names.

To obtain the DECnet address, use the formula:

	(1024*area) + (node_number_within_area)

For example, if a user on the EWS terminal wishes to authorize user FOO on node
DEV (and DEV's DECnet address is 2.15) to create windows on his EWS terminal,
he would add the following in the Motif "Customize Security" box:

	Node:		2063::
	Username:	FOO
	Transport:	DECNET

