>Is there a utility for updating the OpenVMS/OSF console code?

All the firmware CDs I've ever seen, including the aformentioned V2.6,
are pieces of bootable media.  I.E., to do the update, boot your system off
the CD.  At least, that's how it works with VMS systems.  I'm not aware that
it's any different for OSF/1, but since I don't work with it I can't speak to
it
with any certainty.  Perhaps someone with more OSF/1 experience will be kind
enough to support or contradict me as needed.

The boot command will look something like this:

>>> b ddcu -file <filename>

where ddcu is your CD and <filename> is the name of the appropriate update
utility.  Exactly what that is is what you need to track down.

Sorry I can't be more help.  If you don't get anything from here I'm afraid
don't have anything more substantial than "Call the CSC" to suggest.

