> Hi!
> 
> I got a original vt100-terminal (1978) and encountered a few
> (minor) problems.
> 
> I can't get the character-attributes "underline", "blink", "bold" working!
> Just "inverse" works...
> Is that normal?

        The earliest VT100's only do one attribute at a time (choose one
    from INVERSE and UNDERLINE if  memory  serves...it could be a _pair_
    of attributes rather than a single one...).  The local SETUP chooses
    which  you can do.  [Again, this is from memory...I had one of these
    old beasts for a while, but it's been retired for 3 or 4 years so  I
    don't  even  recall  which  setup  is involved, sorry...] Only later
    VT100-series terminals which  support  the ADVANCED_VIDEO option can
    do all four attributes.

> The manual says that all modes should be ok..

        Check carefully.  Does the  manual  mention  the "advanced video
    option" or VT102, etc.?

> Can I switch these modes on?

        You can choose _one_ attribute via the VT100's SETUP.

> Or it is a hardware fault? (No error reported by startup)

        Not likely.  You've just got  a  _very_  old one that doesn't do
    everything you want.  Too bad...

        -Ken
