>
>We have a demo Alpha something-or-other here for a while, and 
>I have been trying to port some common edu software to it. I
>seem to be foiled at every turn!
>
>Are there some common things I need to do to port edu code to Alpha OSF?
>i.e. Am I missing something obvious? Its a demo unit, and we have NO doc.
>No clues in the man pages....


Remember that you're moving to a 64 bit system; it looks suspiciously
like you're encountering problems because of size ambiguities where
the code lucked out on older systems.  Look in the innards of the man
page for lint for help:

  The -Q option provides support for migration from ULTRIX and DEC OSF/1 Ver-
  sion 1.0 systems to DEC OSF/1 Version 1.2.  This option turns on checking
  for all common programming techniques which might cause problems when mov-
  ing from 32-bit systems to 64-bit systems.  The -Q option disables checking
  for other programming problems, so this switch should be used only for
  migration checking.

Then the man page goes on to discuss Q suboptions.  I believe Dec also has
a porting quide in hardcopy available;  ask your sales critter about that.


