The CD coming with the OpenVMS CDD set is in ODS-2 format, and contains a MOP
bootable update system, so the CD need not be physically mounted on every
individual system to update, if VMS systems are present on the LAN.
It's the same AG-PTMWH-BE You have.
Pre-2.6 update disks came with additional hardcopy Firmware release notes, 
the last one has the order number AA-PW8YE-TE. 

In addition to what David F. Wall told, have a look into the OWNERS GUIDE
delivered with the AXP system: it contains detailed instructions how to make the
firmware update on a particular model. In addition to booting the software, You
have to set hardware switches (e.g. inserting the update jumper in a DEC3000).

