I'm using a Dec  Alpha Axp 150 which came with Win/NT preloaded. 
Overall I would say it works very well, although I've had to reboot a couple
of times when the system couldn't see the CDROM for some reason I haven't figured out.
Compatibility mode isn't very fast -- Win16 programs look a bit sluggish.
The monitor is beautiful. It's very sharp in the 1024768 mode.
The system I got came with a 400-odd MB disk drive, which isn't much.
The memory is 32MB, which also isn't much.  After running MS ACCESS 
OR MS WORD or EXCEL, there is only 1 Mbyte free memory.
If I try to run two of those programs, the system goes into
page swap hell.
I haven't ported my particular number crunching program onto the
alpha yet (You need the Win32 SDK -- it's the only compiler available),
so I don't know how this machine really performs in native mode.

-charlie bahr
