	To send any 7-bit or 8-bit code

	Using a VT keyboard (has 20 Function keys across top)
	- Hold down [Compose Character] key
	- Enter code, in decimal, on the Numeric Keypad (right side of kbd)
	- Release [Compose Character] key, code is sent to host

	Using a PC keyboard (has 12 Function keys across top)
	- Hold down [Alt] key
	- Enter code, in decimal, on the Numeric Keypad (right side of kbd)
	- Release [Alt] key, code is sent to host

	Example:  [Alt]+kpd[1]+kpd[1]+kpd[5]  sends CSI.

	You can also enter the character code in column/row format by
pressing the column number of the character as it appears in the character
table, followed by the keypad ".", followed by the row number.

	Example:  [Compose Char]+kpd[6]+kpd[.]+kpd[1]  sends "a" (6/1).

