It is worth noting that the sizes of the four data structures of
interest are (V4.3):

Struct file:   56 bytes
Struct gnode:  248 bytes
Struct proc:   312 bytes
Struct text:   48 bytes

Today you appear to be using about 340 KB in gnode structures.  This
may seem like a lot, but it is just over 1% of the 32 MB.  When you
consider the other things used by the kernel (10% buffer cache),
even doubleing it won't hurt much.  If you are in that desparate
need more memory, get more memory.

The more interesting question to ask is why Pathworks is using up
so many gnodes.  I'd guess that each time a file is opened it keeps
the file opened itself as a sort of cache.  Seem awfully anti-social
though.

