In article <2ikcjk$251@nova.umd.edu>, COATES@UMUC.UMD.EDU (Ellster) writes...
>Please, what is the page size of VMS?

VAX only support a page size of 512 bytes. The Alpha architecture
supports page sizes of 8k, 16k, 32k, and 64k. OpenVMS AXP has been
written to accommodate any of these page sizes. However, all of the
existing Alpha machines have an 8k page size. If you have page size
dependencies in your code, then you should be determining the page size
at run-time. If decisions must be page at compile or link time, you should
assume the "worst case" page size (Alpha images, for instance, create
image sections on 64k page boundaries).

