In article <2ikcjk$251@nova.umd.edu>, COATES@UMUC.UMD.EDU (Ellster) writes:
> Please, what is the page size of VMS?

	Well, that kind of depends.  On a VAX it is 512 bytes / page.
On all current Alpha systems it is 8192 bytes.  Note that the AXP page size
may vary across different AXP systems in the future (8K, 16K, 32K, or 64K).

	To find out what your current system is using for the page size in
bytes, do the following DCL command:

	$ WRITE SYS$OUTPUT F$GETSYI("PAGE_SIZE")

	Or from in a program, use the SYI$_PAGE_SIZE item to a $GETSYI
system service call.

